    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0405" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/>

                <head>No. 200.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokei, Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 31, 1877</date>.
                        (Received June 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 573.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 10th instant a notification that
                    pardon will be granted to such of the insurgents as will lay down their arms,
                    &amp;c, was proclaimed by the imperial army, a translation of which as published
                    in the Japan Herald of date of the 25th instant I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith in duplicate.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d200-a1.xml" xpointer="d200-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
